Classifies each taxon of a phyloseq object into a congruence category by
comparing two \code{tax_table} columns (typically the same taxonomic rank assigned
by two different databases, algorithms or reference sets), and counts both the
number of taxa (ASV/OTU) and the number of sequences (reads) falling in each
category. The five categories are: \code{both_equal} (identical non-missing
assignment), \code{both_na} (missing in both), \verb{only_<rank_1>} (assigned only by
the first column), \verb{only_<rank_2>} (assigned only by the second column), and
\code{different} (both assigned but disagreeing). Empty strings and the literal
values \code{"NA"} / \code{"NA_NA"} are treated as missing.
}
